      "id": "sj4k0fq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is anything that possesses mass and occupies physical space.",
        "The primary physical states of matter are Solid, Liquid, Gas, Plasma, and Bose-Einstein Condensate.",
        "Density measures mass per unit volume and determines whether an object floats or sinks.",
        "Pressure is defined as force applied per unit area and is measured in Pascals (N/m²).",
        "Elasticity is the property of a body to recover its original shape when deforming forces are removed."
      ],
      "id": "60cjn13"
